A||N||7||jaguiler||Air in the system? Overheat?||||1||
Z||000000||jaguiler||05-04-2001||01:56 PM||||Hello,<P>I was changing my coolant sensor.  When I pulled out the old one I notice a good amount of coolant came out...  Then it stopped.... do you think air got in my system when I did that?  I refilled the overflow can and it has been fine......<BR>,..... till today.  <BR>Today I was showing someone my nonfunctioning AC.  I noticed theat my overflow was overflowing.  I had the car idling with AC on for about 7 mintues.  My temp gauge went into the red!  For the first time!  I never got to replace my coolant sensor so I know that is bad, I will soon though....  I let the car cool a little and I turned off the AC... drove around for a minute and the temp gauge dropped to a more normal level.....<P>What happened?  Should I burp the system?  A change in temp doesn't happen that fast does it?<P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||05-04-2001||02:02 PM||||When you pull the sensor out, some coolant will flow out. You did put another sensor in, didn't you? (yeah I know, dumb question)<BR>I think if you just burp your system, you should be ok.<BR>(of course this is coming from a guy that hasn't figured his "overheating" problem out in months)<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||05-04-2001||02:03 PM||||I used my A/C for the first time last week and it overheated.  After checking the fan operation, checking the thermostat in a pot of water with a thermometer, and flushing the system, I finally searched through the archives and found out about "burping" the system.  Since I did that I can't get it to go above 1/4 of the temp guage no matter what I do(a good thing.)  I think any time you lose a little fluid, you should probably burp it, but I'm a total Fiero novice so maybe seek more learned advice.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jaguiler||05-04-2001||02:14 PM||||Considering that I never had an overheating prob before... I will take this route....<P>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000004||firstfiero||05-04-2001||02:50 PM|||| just had that problem. Put a new thermostat in and it got worse. Took it to pep boys thinking I needed a new water pump and they burped the system and now it's all better. I sit at quarter most the time but if I'm in heavy traffic in 90 degree heat...like yesterday....It goes up to about a knotch below half.<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">      <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||14
Z||000005||84Bill||05-04-2001||03:05 PM||||Check out the pics on this thread, I had a frustrating time with overheats and I think this was why.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009918.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009918.html</A> <P>Sqoach<P>You replace your sending unit with a good part? I just noticed my needle is all over the damn whitch way until it warms up then its normal, I'm gonna replace the sending unit and see it that does it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||jaguiler||05-04-2001||05:40 PM||||I went to burp my system just now and discovered I had no thermostat!!!<BR>I have been running like this for about a month and a half now!<BR>oh well I quickly put one in with a new cap as well... the system is running fine...<P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
